godot-docs/issues/10453)\r\n\r\n### What I Did:\r\n- Fixed an issue with string escaping in an example provided for the `OS.shell_open()` method documentation. Now the example is properly escaped to reflect valid Windows path syntax.\r\n- Added a new example of how to open a Windows path using the `OS.shell_open()` method with a different syntax from the first Windows path example.\r\n\r\n### Demonstrations:\r\n- Current Windows path example shown in the `OS.shell_open()` documentation displaying error:\r\n   ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b43d50c-d79f-41dd-b0d3-d2e2ee24ab61)\r\n- Corrected Windows path example showing no errors:\r\n   ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba98cb62-50be-4160-8e32-ef4890f6e1e2)\r\n   - Note: I've tested this GDScript, and it opens the folder as expected. I attached the script to a node and ran the scene, and it worked perfectly. If needed, I can provide a GIF.\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"","color":"ffddff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7008779076,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABocF7RA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/cherrypick:4.3","name":"cherrypick:4.3","description":"Considered for cherry-picking into a future 4.3.x release","color":"446699","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":10558797,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AoR1N","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/20","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/20","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/20/labels","nu